IMPORT prelude

-- Air Navigation Act 1966 (Singapore) -- the offences an ordinary person meets: drones over protected areas, carrying prohibited
-- items and discharging things (ss 32 to 35), unruly passengers and when an aircraft is "in flight" (s 38), trespassing at
-- aerodromes (s 41), the owner's liability for damage caused by aircraft and the immunity from trespass and nuisance (s 42),
-- dangerous flying (s 43), and the cap on composition sums (s 82).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ANA1966.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 3 of 2021 (in force 1 July 2025) and Act 36 of 2018 (in force 1 January 2024) shown. The arrangement of sections at the
-- head of the deposit is out of step with the body; the BODY's section numbers are used throughout.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the offences and liabilities a drone
-- operator, passenger, visitor to an aerodrome, aircraft owner or pilot actually meets. Not encoded: the aviation safety instrument
-- regime (ss 14 to 23), inspection and enforcement powers (ss 24 to 28), reportable safety matters (s 29, which depends wholly on
-- subsidiary legislation), emergency powers (s 31), tampering, dangerous activity and unsafe flights (ss 37, 39, 40), wreck and
-- salvage (s 44), the protection of safety information (ss 45 to 48), air transport and aviation security (Parts 2A, 2B), control
-- of obstructions near aerodromes (Part 3), and the interception of unmanned aircraft (s 90).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Air Navigation Act 1966 -- offences`

§§ `32 to 35 -- unmanned aircraft`

-- s 32(1): the Minister may by order in the Gazette declare any area to be a protected area.
-- s 32(2): if an unmanned aircraft "has on board equipment for taking photographs when flying" and a photograph is taken of the whole
-- or any part of a protected area using it, "the operator of the unmanned aircraft, and the person taking the photograph if the
-- person is not the operator, shall each be guilty of an offence". (7): taking a photograph includes making a film or video recording
-- and recording images for broadcasting or live-streaming.
-- (5)(a): the prosecution need not prove the accused knew the area was protected or that the drone had a camera; (b) defence, on a
-- balance of probabilities: (i) the photograph "was not taken intentionally but was taken because of weather conditions or other
-- unavoidable cause"; or (ii) a permit from a competent security officer, and the photograph taken in accordance with it.
--
-- s 33(1): "A person must not operate an unmanned aircraft to fly, at any height, over any part of any protected area"; (2) every
-- OPERATOR who contravenes is guilty. (5)(a) knowledge of the protected area need not be proved; (b) defence: (i) the accused "did not
-- intentionally cause the unmanned aircraft to fly over the protected area, and the overflight was not due to any want of reasonable
-- care"; or (ii) the overflight was authorised by and in accordance with a permit from a competent security officer.
--
-- s 34(1): operating an unmanned aircraft "indoors or at any height over any area in Singapore" while it carries a prohibited item.
-- (2) knowledge need not be proved; defence: the accused "did not know, and could not reasonably have been expected to know".
-- (4) prohibited item: weapons and substances whose possession is an offence under the Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021
-- or the Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act 1958; biological agents and toxins; radioactive material; and
-- hazardous material prescribed by Gazette notification.
--
-- s 35(1): operating an unmanned aircraft indoors or over any area in Singapore which "discharges anything (whether gaseous, liquid or
-- solid)". (8): discharge "includes dropping ... but does not include the discharge of exhaust". (4) defences: (a) not intentional
-- AND not due to want of reasonable care AND all reasonably practicable steps taken to stop further discharge; (b) escape after
-- damage "other than intentional damage" with all reasonable precautions taken; (c) a discharge permit from the Authority, followed.
-- (5): "it is not a defence" that no one died or was hurt, no property was damaged, or no hazard was caused.
DECLARE `Drone incident` HAS
    `the person is the operator`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person took the photograph`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knew the area was protected`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `photographed a protected area from the drone`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `photo was unintended, by weather or unavoidable cause`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `flew over a protected area`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `overflight was intentional`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `took reasonable care`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `acted under a security officer's permit`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `carried a prohibited item`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `could reasonably have known of the item`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `discharged something`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the discharge was only exhaust`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the discharge was intentional`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `took all practicable steps to stop further discharge`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `escaped after unintended damage, precautions taken`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `acted under a discharge permit`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `nobody was hurt and nothing was damaged`                   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the incident` IS A `Drone incident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the photography offence is committed` IF
        `the incident`'s `photographed a protected area from the drone`
    AND (`the incident`'s `the person is the operator` OR `the incident`'s `the person took the photograph`)
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `photo was unintended, by weather or unavoidable cause`)
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `acted under a security officer's permit`)

GIVEN `the incident` IS A `Drone incident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the overflight offence is committed` IF
        `the incident`'s `flew over a protected area`
    AND `the incident`'s `the person is the operator`
    AND (NOT ((NOT `the incident`'s `overflight was intentional`) AND `the incident`'s `took reasonable care`))
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `acted under a security officer's permit`)

GIVEN `the incident` IS A `Drone incident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prohibited item offence is committed` IF
        `the incident`'s `carried a prohibited item`
    AND `the incident`'s `the person is the operator`
    AND `the incident`'s `could reasonably have known of the item`

GIVEN `the incident` IS A `Drone incident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge defence is made out` IF
        (     (NOT `the incident`'s `the discharge was intentional`)
          AND `the incident`'s `took reasonable care`
          AND `the incident`'s `took all practicable steps to stop further discharge`)
    OR  `the incident`'s `escaped after unintended damage, precautions taken`
    OR  `the incident`'s `acted under a discharge permit`

GIVEN `the incident` IS A `Drone incident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge offence is committed` IF
        `the incident`'s `discharged something`
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `the discharge was only exhaust`)
    AND `the incident`'s `the person is the operator`
    AND (NOT (`the discharge defence is made out` `the incident`))

-- Penalties. ss 32(3), 33(3), 35(2): a fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both; "where the person is a
-- repeat offender", $100,000 or 5 years or both. A repeat offender has been convicted or found guilty "on at least one other earlier
-- occasion" of an offence under the SAME subsection (ss 32(4), 33(4), 35(3)). s 34(1): $100,000 or 5 years, with no repeat tier.
-- Imprisonment is in months.
DECLARE `Drone offence` IS ONE OF
    `photographing a protected area`
    `flying over a protected area`
    `carrying a prohibited item`
    `discharging from a drone`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Drone offence`, `earlier convictions for the same offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum drone fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying a prohibited item` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE
        IF `earlier convictions for the same offence` AT LEAST 1 THEN 100000 ELSE 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Drone offence`, `earlier convictions for the same offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum drone imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying a prohibited item` THEN 60
    OTHERWISE
        IF `earlier convictions for the same offence` AT LEAST 1 THEN 60 ELSE 24

§§ `38 -- unruly passengers`

-- s 38(6): an aircraft is in flight "from the time when all external doors of the aircraft are closed following embarkation for a
-- flight until the time when any such door is opened for disembarkation"; after a forced landing abroad, until the competent
-- authorities there "take over responsibility"; after a forced landing in Singapore, "until the time when a police officer arrives at
-- the place of landing".
GIVEN `all external doors closed after embarkation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a door opened for disembarkation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `forced landing in Singapore and police arrived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `forced landing abroad and local authorities took over` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aircraft is in flight` IF
        `all external doors closed after embarkation`
    AND (NOT `a door opened for disembarkation`)
    AND (NOT `forced landing in Singapore and police arrived`)
    AND (NOT `forced landing abroad and local authorities took over`)

-- s 38(1): while in an aircraft in flight, (a) interfering with a crew member performing duties connected with safe operation, (b)
-- behaving "in a threatening, offensive, insulting or disorderly manner towards a crew member", or (c) threatening the safety of the
-- aircraft or persons on board -- $100,000 or 5 years or both.
-- (2): failing to comply with commands of the pilot-in-command, given directly or through a crew member, for safe operation in flight
-- -- $100,000 or 5 years or both.
-- (3): (a) boarding so intoxicated as to be incapable of looking after oneself, or as to jeopardise good order and discipline; (b)
-- becoming so intoxicated on board an aircraft in flight -- $20,000 or 12 months or both. (5) defence: intoxicated "not because of
-- being under the influence of any alcohol, drugs or other intoxicating substances", or by "prescription medication in accordance
-- with a medical authorisation".
-- (4): (a) operating a portable electronic device in breach of aviation safety subsidiary legislation; (b) smoking when instructed not
-- to by a crew member or a sign or placard -- $5,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE `Conduct on board` IS ONE OF
    `interfering with a crew member's safety duties`
    `insulting or threatening a crew member`
    `threatening the safety of the aircraft`
    `disobeying the pilot-in-command's safety command`
    `boarding while dangerously drunk`
    `becoming dangerously drunk in flight`
    `using a device against the rules`
    `smoking after being told not to`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct on board`,
      `the aircraft was in flight` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intoxicated without alcohol, drugs or intoxicants` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intoxicated by authorised prescription medication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under s 38` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `interfering with a crew member's safety duties` THEN `the aircraft was in flight`
    WHEN `insulting or threatening a crew member` THEN `the aircraft was in flight`
    WHEN `threatening the safety of the aircraft` THEN `the aircraft was in flight`
    WHEN `boarding while dangerously drunk` THEN
        (NOT `intoxicated without alcohol, drugs or intoxicants`) AND (NOT `intoxicated by authorised prescription medication`)
    WHEN `becoming dangerously drunk in flight` THEN
        `the aircraft was in flight` AND (NOT `intoxicated without alcohol, drugs or intoxicants`) AND (NOT `intoxicated by authorised prescription medication`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct on board`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 38 fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `boarding while dangerously drunk` THEN 20000
    WHEN `becoming dangerously drunk in flight` THEN 20000
    WHEN `using a device against the rules` THEN 5000
    WHEN `smoking after being told not to` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 100000

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct on board`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 38 imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `boarding while dangerously drunk` THEN 12
    WHEN `becoming dangerously drunk in flight` THEN 12
    WHEN `using a device against the rules` THEN 12
    WHEN `smoking after being told not to` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 60

§§ `41 -- trespassing at aerodromes`

-- s 41(1): "A person must not, without prior authorisation from the Authority" enter or remain in, leave property on, drive a
-- vehicle on, or bring or let an animal or bird onto, a prohibited area within an aerodrome. (2) fine not exceeding $5,000 -- no
-- imprisonment. (4) "prohibited area" means any part of the aerodrome "upon which is posted a notice" that trespassing is prohibited,
-- "purporting to have been posted with the authority of the Authority". (3) arrest and removal without warrant (not encoded).
GIVEN `entered a part of an aerodrome` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a no-trespassing notice of the Authority was posted there` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had prior authorisation from the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aerodrome trespass offence is committed` IF
        `entered a part of an aerodrome`
    AND `a no-trespassing notice of the Authority was posted there`
    AND (NOT `had prior authorisation from the Authority`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum aerodrome trespass fine` MEANS 5000

§§ `42 -- trespass, nuisance and damage`

-- s 42(1): "no action lies in respect of trespass or in respect of nuisance, by reason only of the flight of aircraft over any
-- property at a height above the ground which ... is reasonable", so long as Part 2 and its subsidiary legislation "are duly complied
-- with".
GIVEN `the height was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `Part 2 and its regulations were complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action for overflight trespass or nuisance is barred` IF
    `the height was reasonable` AND `Part 2 and its regulations were complied with`

-- s 42(2): material damage or loss caused by an aircraft in flight, taking off or landing, by a person in it, or by an article
-- falling from it, to any person or property on land or water -- damages are recoverable from the owner "without proof of negligence
-- or intention or other cause of action", "except where the damage or loss was caused by or contributed to by the negligence of the
-- person by whom the damage or loss was suffered". The exception reads as a complete bar, not an apportionment.
GIVEN `material damage on the ground caused by the aircraft or something falling from it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim's own negligence caused or contributed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages are recoverable without proof of fault` IF
    `material damage on the ground caused by the aircraft or something falling from it`
    AND (NOT `the victim's own negligence caused or contributed`)

-- s 42(4): where the aircraft has been "bona fide demised, let, or hired out for a period exceeding 14 days" and no pilot, commander,
-- navigator or operative crew member is in the owner's employment, the section reads as though the hirer were the owner.
DECLARE `Liable party` IS ONE OF
    `the owner`
    `the hirer`

GIVEN `days hired out` IS A NUMBER, `any operative crew employed by the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Liable party`
`who answers under s 42` MEANS
    IF `days hired out` GREATER THAN 14 AND (NOT `any operative crew employed by the owner`)
    THEN `the hirer`
    ELSE `the owner`

§§ `43 -- dangerous flying`

-- s 43(1): where an aircraft is flown "so as to be the cause of unnecessary danger to any person or property on land or water", the
-- pilot or person in charge "and also the owner of the aircraft, unless he, she or it proves ... that the aircraft was so flown without
-- his, her or its actual fault or privity" -- $100,000 or 5 years or both. (2) "owner" includes "any person by whom the aircraft is
-- hired at the time of the offence".
DECLARE `Person connected with the aircraft` IS ONE OF
    `the pilot or person in charge`
    `the owner`
    `the hirer at the time`
    `a passenger`

GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person connected with the aircraft`,
      `flown so as to cause unnecessary danger on the ground` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no actual fault or privity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty of dangerous flying` IF
    `flown so as to cause unnecessary danger on the ground` AND
    (CONSIDER `the person`
     WHEN `the pilot or person in charge` THEN TRUE
     WHEN `the owner` THEN NOT `proved no actual fault or privity`
     WHEN `the hirer at the time` THEN NOT `proved no actual fault or privity`
     OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `82 -- compounding`

-- s 82(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a)
-- "one-half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (b) "$5,000". (2) on payment no further
-- proceedings. (3) the Minister prescribes which offences are compoundable (the rules were not retrieved).
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum offered` IS A NUMBER, `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for that sum` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum offered` AT MOST `the most that may be collected to compound` `maximum fine`
